cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ephapax"
abstract: "Research language exploring dyadic linear/affine typing, region-based allocation, and WebAssembly. Includes Coq and Idris2 proof artifacts; current counterexamples refute unrestricted legacy and L1 preservation, no unconditional L2 preservation theorem is established, and implementation refinement remains unproved."
